## Hints

- E2: expected cost = P(fund|null)·2M·(base of nulls) + P(pass|real)·
  8M·(base of reals) — the base rates matter; assume 90% nulls.
- E4: n = ((1.645+0.84)·σ/δ)²; dividing σ by √30 divides n by 30 —
  diversification is a data multiplier.
